      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>SCHEDULE E - LINE 4</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>PURPOSE: THE WASHINGTON ELEMENTARY SCHOOL FOUNDATION ENHANCES AND EXPANDS THE EDUCATIONAL PROGRAM, AT WASHINGTON S.T.E.A.M. MAGNET, BY SPONSORING EXTENDED LEARNING OPPORTUNITIES, AS WELL AS EXCURSIONS INTO, AND PARTICIPATION IN, THE LOCAL COMMUNITY AND CULTURE. WE COORDINATE AND SPONSOR LEADERSHIP OPPORTUNITIES FOR OUR OLDER STUDENTS SUCH AS THE SAFETY PATROL, AFTERSCHOOL CLUBS, AND STUDENT BUSINESSES. OUR PREMIER EVENT, VAN-GO HELPS TO BOTH PROMOTE OUR SCHOOL AND DEFINE US AS THE FINES S.T.E.A.M. (SCIENCE, TECHNOLOGY, ENGINEERING, ARTS, AND MATHEMATICS) SCHOOL IN CALIFORNIA. ACCOMPLISHMENTS: WASHINGTON ELEMENTARY FOUNDATION HAS PROVIDED AFTER SCHOOL TUTORING TO STUDENTS, PROVIDED ADDITONAL RESOURCE TEACHERS TO WORK IN SMALL GROUPS WITH HIGH RISK STUDENTS AND THOSE WITH GREATER ACADEMIC NEEDS AND HAS ALSO HAD THE OPPORTUNITY TO PAY FOR AFTER SCHOOL ENRICHMENT CLUBS SUCH AS MUSIC, THEATRE, SCIENCE, SPORTS AND TECHNOLOGY.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
